    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (72.82) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.32) serve as our offensive pillars. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Kumar Rocker, where a 10% park boost combined with a 13% dynamic platoon advantage creates an ideal environment for power production. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start despite facing Michael King; his score is buoyed by a 10% SP skill adjustment and the inherent value of his spot in the order, though we are tracking his SB potential closely against an elite hold pitcher. We are also looking for high-floor contributions from **Gleyber Torres** (59.94) and **Zack Gelof** (58.96), both of whom capitalize on favorable lineup positioning and park factors to comfortably clear our 50-point threshold.\n\nThe tightest decision of the day involved **Jeremiah Jackson**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a 46.43 score. While his potential for stolen bases\u2014aided by a \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus\u2014is attractive, he ultimately lost out to the superior platoon and park adjustments afforded to players like **Daulton Varsho** (58.93) and **Brendan Donovan** (57.67). We remain cautious regarding **Yainer Diaz** (44.60) and **Masyn Winn** (48.78); **Yainer Diaz** is hampered by an unfavorable #9 hole projection, while **Masyn Winn** faces a wind-in scenario that tempers his offensive ceiling. With lineups still pending for several key hitters, the primary risk remains a cascade of late-scratches that would force us to pivot from our projected order, potentially destabilizing the narrow efficiency gains we\u2019ve identified for **Jung Hoo Lee** (51.14) and **Dylan Beavers** (50.24).",
